# render_objects_placement: Placements (section 6.11): a service task with argument buffers takes a placement list with its object list (opcode 68), and the state objects read and write their entries. A depth-stencil state zeroes its entry's first word; a pipeline with a nonzero resourceID is created at the entry's resourceIndex, one with resourceID 0 wherever Metal puts it; a sampler with a nonzero resourceIndex whose gpuResourceID comes out different fails ("Failed to create sampler state with correct resourceID"), one with index 0 is not checked, and one with argument-buffer support writes its entry back (those values are the host's, so not dumped). Isolate only: in-process tasks never get a placement list.
